1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,320
This is a review guide

2
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:03,400
for the foosball goal counters:

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,120
what the change adds, how to review it,

4
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,145
and where to start reading.

5
00:00:08,145 --> 00:00:09,905
Nothing is merged yet.

6
00:00:09,905 --> 00:00:12,785
The work splits into four pull requests:

7
00:00:12,785 --> 00:00:13,825
the API,

8
00:00:13,825 --> 00:00:15,985
the beta frontend and its docs,

9
00:00:15,985 --> 00:00:19,149
the hardware folder, and observability.

10
00:00:19,549 --> 00:00:21,069
A ball breaks an infrared

11
00:00:21,069 --> 00:00:22,749
beam in the goal's drawer.

12
00:00:22,749 --> 00:00:24,589
The counter saves the goal,

13
00:00:24,589 --> 00:00:27,878
beeps, and posts it to the API.

14
00:00:27,878 --> 00:00:29,878
The API stores the goal,

15
00:00:29,878 --> 00:00:31,558
bumps the table's version,

16
00:00:31,558 --> 00:00:32,998
and wakes every phone

17
00:00:32,998 --> 00:00:35,226
that is waiting on that table.

18
00:00:35,226 --> 00:00:37,386
The phone shows the new score,

19
00:00:37,386 --> 00:00:40,078
usually within a second of the goal.

20
00:00:40,078 --> 00:00:42,398
Undo comes from one place only:

21
00:00:42,398 --> 00:00:44,158
the counter's own button,

22
00:00:44,158 --> 00:00:47,498
for its own goal, within ten seconds.

23
00:00:47,898 --> 00:00:50,538
Pull request one is the API.

24
00:00:50,538 --> 00:00:53,338
Devices sign in with their own scheme.

25
00:00:53,338 --> 00:00:54,618
An unknown device

26
00:00:54,618 --> 00:00:56,511
that holds the organisation's

27
00:00:56,511 --> 00:00:58,858
enrolment token registers itself,

28
00:00:58,858 --> 00:01:00,058
unclaimed.

29
00:01:00,058 --> 00:01:02,938
After that, only its own secret counts,

30
00:01:02,938 --> 00:01:05,315
compared in constant time.

31
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:06,595
The device endpoints

32
00:01:06,595 --> 00:01:10,675
live under /api/v3/hardware.

33
00:01:10,675 --> 00:01:12,515
They stay out of Swagger:

34
00:01:12,515 --> 00:01:16,780
their contract is the firmware's OpenAPI file.

35
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:19,920
A goal event returns 201 when it is counted,

36
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:23,740
409 for a retry the server has already seen,

37
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:26,540
and 422 when the event belongs

38
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:28,331
to another device.

39
00:01:28,331 --> 00:01:30,411
The undo rules sit in one place,

40
00:01:30,411 --> 00:01:31,931
inside the table lock.

41
00:01:31,931 --> 00:01:34,491
A retry is deduplicated first.

42
00:01:34,491 --> 00:01:37,051
Then come the refusals: not yours,

43
00:01:37,051 --> 00:01:40,091
game closed, already undone, or too late.

44
00:01:40,091 --> 00:01:43,018
Each is a 422 with a code.

45
00:01:43,018 --> 00:01:45,098
The live view is a long-poll.

46
00:01:45,098 --> 00:01:46,698
Send the version you have.

47
00:01:46,698 --> 00:01:49,738
If the table has changed, you get it at once.

48
00:01:49,738 --> 00:01:53,139
If not, the request waits for the next change.

49
00:01:53,139 --> 00:01:55,619
Every change to a table takes one path:

50
00:01:55,619 --> 00:01:56,659
lock the row,

51
00:01:56,659 --> 00:01:58,979
apply the change, bump the version,

52
00:01:58,979 --> 00:02:00,899
commit, then notify.

53
00:02:00,899 --> 00:02:02,339
One limit to know:

54
00:02:02,339 --> 00:02:04,019
waiters also re-check the

55
00:02:04,019 --> 00:02:05,859
database every two seconds,

56
00:02:05,859 --> 00:02:08,739
so several API replicas still work,

57
00:02:08,739 --> 00:02:10,556
just a little slower.

58
00:02:10,556 --> 00:02:12,956
Two small background services save

59
00:02:12,956 --> 00:02:15,036
a won game after ten seconds,

60
00:02:15,036 --> 00:02:17,968
and close games that have gone quiet.

61
00:02:17,968 --> 00:02:20,448
One migration adds eight tables.

62
00:02:20,448 --> 00:02:22,448
Two unique indexes matter:

63
00:02:22,448 --> 00:02:24,768
a goal event is stored only once,

64
00:02:24,768 --> 00:02:27,897
and only one counter can guard each goal.

65
00:02:27,897 --> 00:02:30,137
Every table now belongs to one league,

66
00:02:30,137 --> 00:02:32,057
and so do its devices.

67
00:02:32,057 --> 00:02:33,417
Its games are claimed

68
00:02:33,417 --> 00:02:35,417
and rated only in that league:

69
00:02:35,417 --> 00:02:37,577
another league gets a 400.

70
00:02:37,577 --> 00:02:39,737
And a table can change league only

71
00:02:39,737 --> 00:02:41,337
when no game is live,

72
00:02:41,337 --> 00:02:43,586
or waiting for its players.

73
00:02:43,586 --> 00:02:46,146
The seed data gives you two tables,

74
00:02:46,146 --> 00:02:49,346
six placeholder devices in every health state,

75
00:02:49,346 --> 00:02:51,746
a live game with an undone goal,

76
00:02:51,746 --> 00:02:52,946
and a finished game

77
00:02:52,946 --> 00:02:55,286
that is waiting for its players.

78
00:02:55,286 --> 00:02:59,366
The API suite now has 294 integration

79
00:02:59,366 --> 00:03:03,509
tests. 57 of them are new hardware tests.

80
00:03:03,509 --> 00:03:06,309
Start with the hardware API document,

81
00:03:06,309 --> 00:03:07,989
then the device controller,

82
00:03:07,989 --> 00:03:09,589
the authentication handler,

83
00:03:09,589 --> 00:03:12,081
and the table match service.

84
00:03:12,481 --> 00:03:15,201
Pull request two is the beta frontend.

85
00:03:15,201 --> 00:03:18,241
The table page becomes the phone's live view:

86
00:03:18,241 --> 00:03:21,514
the score, who scored last, and when.

87
00:03:21,514 --> 00:03:23,834
The page holds one request at a time,

88
00:03:23,834 --> 00:03:25,914
and never repeats a held one.

89
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:28,794
A goal makes the scoring column pulse.

90
00:03:28,794 --> 00:03:32,361
An undo shows a short line with the new score.

91
00:03:32,361 --> 00:03:35,081
New game sends the version the phone saw.

92
00:03:35,081 --> 00:03:37,961
A stale screen gets a polite conflict,

93
00:03:37,961 --> 00:03:40,370
instead of ending the wrong game.

94
00:03:40,370 --> 00:03:43,090
The admin Hardware page sets up tables,

95
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:46,290
their league and team names, claims new devices,

96
00:03:46,290 --> 00:03:48,930
and asks one question per goal counter:

97
00:03:48,930 --> 00:03:51,537
whose goalkeeper guards this goal?

98
00:03:51,537 --> 00:03:54,257
Each device shows its health: battery,

99
00:03:54,257 --> 00:03:56,897
silence, and the beam's own checks.

100
00:03:56,897 --> 00:03:58,577
The admin overview leads

101
00:03:58,577 --> 00:04:00,698
with whatever needs attention.

102
00:04:00,698 --> 00:04:02,378
A game the table scored can

103
00:04:02,378 --> 00:04:04,298
be claimed from the submit page,

104
00:04:04,298 --> 00:04:06,378
or from the table's short link.

105
00:04:06,378 --> 00:04:09,561
Then it is rated like any other match.

106
00:04:09,561 --> 00:04:11,881
There are 45 new Vitest tests,

107
00:04:11,881 --> 00:04:13,561
and a new Playwright spec

108
00:04:13,561 --> 00:04:16,601
with 7 end-to-end tests for the live view

109
00:04:16,601 --> 00:04:18,281
and the admin page.

110
00:04:18,281 --> 00:04:20,921
Please run the beta's end-to-end suite

111
00:04:20,921 --> 00:04:22,498
before you approve.

112
00:04:22,498 --> 00:04:25,938
Start with the table page, then live.ts,

113
00:04:25,938 --> 00:04:29,769
then the admin Hardware page and device health.

114
00:04:30,169 --> 00:04:32,969
Pull request three is the hardware folder.

115
00:04:32,969 --> 00:04:34,329
The firmware keeps all of

116
00:04:34,329 --> 00:04:35,689
its behaviour in a core

117
00:04:35,689 --> 00:04:38,729
that also builds and tests on your laptop.

118
00:04:38,729 --> 00:04:41,058
The device layer is thin.

119
00:04:41,058 --> 00:04:44,178
A goal is a beam that stays blocked long enough.

120
00:04:44,178 --> 00:04:46,978
It is counted while the ball is still there,

121
00:04:46,978 --> 00:04:48,498
then locked out briefly,

122
00:04:48,498 --> 00:04:50,923
so one ball counts once.

123
00:04:50,923 --> 00:04:52,603
Each goal is saved to flash

124
00:04:52,603 --> 00:04:53,883
before anything is sent,

125
00:04:53,883 --> 00:04:56,123
and the counter beeps at once.

126
00:04:56,123 --> 00:04:58,463
No beep means no goal.

127
00:04:58,463 --> 00:05:02,063
An undo joins the same queue, behind its goal,

128
00:05:02,063 --> 00:05:04,783
so the server always sees them in order.

129
00:05:04,783 --> 00:05:06,543
The server's answer comes back

130
00:05:06,543 --> 00:05:08,243
to the little screen.

131
00:05:08,243 --> 00:05:09,763
The digital twin compiles

132
00:05:09,763 --> 00:05:11,603
that same core for your laptop,

133
00:05:11,603 --> 00:05:14,643
and runs 19 scenarios against the mock server

134
00:05:14,643 --> 00:05:16,563
or the real API:

135
00:05:16,563 --> 00:05:18,683
power cuts, offline queues,

136
00:05:18,683 --> 00:05:21,159
stuck balls, and daylight.

137
00:05:21,159 --> 00:05:23,479
The sled is parametric CAD

138
00:05:23,479 --> 00:05:25,079
with its own self-check.

139
00:05:25,079 --> 00:05:27,239
An assembly gate moves every

140
00:05:27,239 --> 00:05:28,839
part along its real path

141
00:05:28,839 --> 00:05:29,575
into place:

142
00:05:29,575 --> 00:05:33,350
139 checks, all passing.

143
00:05:33,350 --> 00:05:36,710
On the firmware side: 55 native tests,

144
00:05:36,710 --> 00:05:38,710
and 30 contract payloads

145
00:05:38,710 --> 00:05:41,935
checked against the OpenAPI file.

146
00:05:41,935 --> 00:05:44,015
Start with the interfaces document,

147
00:05:44,015 --> 00:05:46,575
then the firmware README and the goal app,

148
00:05:46,575 --> 00:05:48,352
then the twin.

149
00:05:48,752 --> 00:05:51,392
Pull request four is observability.

150
00:05:51,392 --> 00:05:53,792
Aspire gains a Grafana container

151
00:05:53,792 --> 00:05:55,712
that you start when you want it.

152
00:05:55,712 --> 00:05:58,272
Devices send their logs and metrics

153
00:05:58,272 --> 00:06:01,924
with OpenTelemetry at the end of each session.

154
00:06:01,924 --> 00:06:03,444
There are two dashboards,

155
00:06:03,444 --> 00:06:05,684
one for the fleet and one per device,

156
00:06:05,684 --> 00:06:07,444
and eight alert rules,

157
00:06:07,444 --> 00:06:08,644
from a low battery

158
00:06:08,644 --> 00:06:11,085
to a blocked beam during play.

159
00:06:11,085 --> 00:06:13,325
The OTLP port has no authentication,

160
00:06:13,325 --> 00:06:16,765
so it stays on localhost unless you opt in.

161
00:06:16,765 --> 00:06:18,860
Nothing is deployed.

162
00:06:18,860 --> 00:06:21,100
Start with the observability README,

163
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,380
then the AppHost,

164
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:26,365
the alert rules, and the device's OTLP code.

165
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:29,932
A few things deserve a closer look.

166
00:06:29,932 --> 00:06:32,572
The scoreboard is parked, not removed:

167
00:06:32,572 --> 00:06:36,012
its endpoints and pages are still in the API

168
00:06:36,012 --> 00:06:37,372
and the frontend.

169
00:06:37,372 --> 00:06:39,692
The two changesets also mention it,

170
00:06:39,692 --> 00:06:41,772
and they are longer than our usual one

171
00:06:41,772 --> 00:06:43,675
or two sentences.

172
00:06:43,675 --> 00:06:45,088
And check the long-poll's

173
00:06:45,088 --> 00:06:48,050
two-second fallback under load.

174
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:50,690
Four pull requests, one feature:

175
00:06:50,690 --> 00:06:52,210
goals counted in the drawer,

176
00:06:52,210 --> 00:06:54,210
and shown live on the phone.

177
00:06:54,210 --> 00:06:56,126
Thanks for reviewing.
